# STIG AS24-U1-000520: The Apache web server must generate a session ID using as mu
# STIG ID: V-214253 (HIGH)

META
    esp_id `apache-as24-u1-000520-unique-id-module-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `apache`
    criticality `critical`

    title `STIG AS24-U1-000520: The Apache web server must generate a session ID using as much of the character `
    description `The Apache web server must generate a session ID using as much of the character set as possible to reduce the risk of brute force.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `apache,stig,disa-stig,module`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:AS24-U1-000520,NIST-800-53:SC-23(3)`
    control_objective `SC-23(3)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Apache:localhost:web-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA Apache STIG guidance for AS24-U1-000520.`

    component_id `comp-apache-web`

    impl_SC_23_3 `This control is validated by checking the Apache HTTP server configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT module_check
        module `unique_id_module`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE module_state
        loaded boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN apache_module
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF module_state
            OBJECT_REF module_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
